- **G-1 closure of round 1 (R1).** B619-1 (V3, a null supplies link treated as an empty link) NOT killed by at least one committed row that is green at the unmutated head = **Major (same class: cap)**. B619-2 (V2, the skip widened to the empty string, both edits) not killed = **Major (same class)**. B619-3 (V4, `device.Cells is null` returns true) not killed = **Major (same class)** (it was Minor in round 1; in round 2 it was commissioned into the class, so a survivor is a Major). The V3 control (zero-cost device, link `""`, validates, 200 `Validating`) red or absent = **Major**. A closure that holds only under the builder's definition of the mutant and not under yours (rebuilt from B619 STATUS lines 20-22 and the commission text, not from the builder's tables) = Major.
- **G-2 survivor hunt (R4; the cap).** A mutant of the two validator edits (the skip in the first-row build, the skip in the group walk, the null-link branch) or of line `:203` that changes the behaviour of some staged document through the governed validate and survives the whole `SourceLifecycleTests` family (324 expected) AND the Import `ReferenceDocumentValidator` family = **Major (same class)**, unless a forced run shows it unreachable through every input path (then Minor, with the proof). Proven-equivalent mutants (V4d, V12, c3) go in their own list with the reason. A survivor of an adjacent existing line outside the class (no committed change) = Minor, ticket-shaped.
- **G-3 the rows (R3).** An existing row or assertion edited, removed, skipped or loosened (a removed line) = **Major** (always; expected 0). A new case whose expectation is read from the code under test (the `GovernedNullClassExpected` table and every list must be TYPED; the helper must not call the validator or import its constants for the expected side) = Major. A case red for another reason than it names, or green at the source that the builder says is red (or the reverse) = Major. A case no mutant turns red and that is not a declared control = Major (the builder says 0; the four Set A controls are killed only by V3c, an own mutant: judge whether V3c is a real regression, say so). A name lost, or a name added beyond the 91 = Major. A case that depends on the machine (culture, zone, clock, port, environment variable, writable path outside the temp area, test order, unseeded random) or leaves a directory behind = Minor (Major if it can fail on a Linux runner). The expected `(location | rule)` literals re-derived by YOUR run: a literal that differs from your measurement at the unmodified head = Major.
- **G-4 B619-6 siblings (R6).** A shape listed in B619 STATUS line 25 that no new case pins = Note (carried) unless a mutant of it survives (then G-2). The both-products-nulled answer (`DUPLICATE_SOFTWARE_TERM` at `softwareRows[5..9]`, builder STATUS line 208) is a new measurement: confirm it by your run; it is the existing code and rule, so a Note.
- **G-5 delta, scope and claims.** Always **Blocker**: a path beyond the one new file in the round-2 commit; ANY byte under `src`, `docs`, `web`, `.github` or a contract differing from `34ccb02`; the head moved; a removed line. Always **Major**: a builder claim your measurement contradicts (91 cases, +411 -0, 106 on the narrow filter, 324 on `SourceLifecycleTests`, Api 2,963, the V2/V3/V4/V2a/V2b/V2w/V3b/V4c kill counts 5/4/8/5/5/10/10/4, V4d 0, N1-N6 71/68/10/10/41/68, c0/c1/c2 0 red, names lost 0 added 91, 0 warnings). **Always Note:** the builder's process disclosures (the `rm -f` of its own canary file; the arithmetic slip 95 vs 91; the unproven serial-run flag), CI state stated, the squash message choice, style.
- **G-6 hygiene.** A real price, BID value, SKU, description or any value from a real book in an added line, the commit message, your STATUS or your evidence = **Blocker**; a person's name, a secret, a customer datum = **Blocker**; a ticket key, a decision-card id, a gate finding id (`B619-n`), a mutant id (`V2`, `N1`), a brief number or a percent figure in the new file's code lines, test names or the commit message = Major; non-ASCII in added lines = Major; a build warning = Major; a skipped, failed or `Skip =` test = **Blocker**. A decimal literal in a price shape = Minor. The word "only" or "skipped" inside a comment is not a finding.
- **G-7 CI and CodeQL (R5).** A failing check-run on the head or merge result = **Major**; a warning, failed or skipped test in the whole line = **Blocker**; an analysis missing (4 of 4 required) = Major; a NEW open alert on the PR ref (a number absent from main's open list) with security severity high or higher, or rule severity `error` = **Blocker** (both thresholds of ruleset 24139430); below both = Minor; a check `in_progress` at the verdict: the verdict line says `CI pending: <names>` and is at most GO WITH FINDINGS.
- **G-8 overlap and merge.** A path shared with a live lane or open PR other than #110 = Major (expected 0; #111 shares none); a conflict marker in the legacy `merge-tree` = Major for the merge order (Tuesday's call); a merge result tree differing from the head tree while main equals base = Major (a harness fault to explain).
- **Verdict token.** GO needs every check-run at the head completed and green, 4 of 4 analyses with both CodeQL thresholds met, the whole line green, R1 and R4 closed (no Major), 0 findings above Note. GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note only. **NO GO** = any Blocker or Major; the line lists every Major+ by id and says for each whether it is the SAME CLASS as B619-1/-2/-3. A required check you could not run makes the first and last lines add ` (conditional: <reason>)`, never a bare GO; an R4 whose power control failed is always conditional.

## LOAD (binding; the MPS heavy-slot convention, RELAYED from B619 and its templates)
8 cores; load1 reads 7-11 tonight. Heavy = `dotnet build`, `dotnet test`, `dotnet test --list-tests`, `dotnet restore`, a mutant run, the full CI line. **Start a heavy run only while `uptime` load1 is below 7** at two reads 4 s apart (not independent: the figure refreshes about every 5 s; say so), recorded beside the result; at 7 or over poll every 20 s, log each wait, and do light work meanwhile (R2 reading, hygiene, R7 by GitHub, predictions, the tokenizer and multiset programs, reading the new file). **Then take ONE slot atomically:** `mkdir '<project root>/.tools/heavy-slot-1' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '<project root>/.tools/heavy-slot-2' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '<project root>/.tools/heavy-slot-3'`, write `B645 <start time> <label>` into its `holder`; read every other holder first (drafter, 08:39: `heavy-slot-1` is G105's; read them fresh; a holder that looks stale is reported, never removed or moved; a slot directory with no holder file is reported, never taken over). All taken: wait 3 minutes and retry. At most ONE slot, one heavy job at a time; re-read load1 at the start of EACH job inside a held slot; for a run longer than a few minutes also hold a seat-local lock directory `.tools/b645/heavy.lock` (pid inside, released by a MOVE); at the run's end release ONLY your own slot, by a MOVE into `.tools/_quarantine/2026-10-25_B645_<slot>_<label>/`, never `rm`. The shared `.tools/.git-lock` (atomic `mkdir`, read any holder first) wraps GIT REF WRITES ONLY (your clone's one `fetch`, `worktree add`). **A MOVING heartbeat** (a counter plus `date`) goes to `.tools/b645/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job; a figure that does not move for 3 beats means the waiter is stuck: say so. **A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` or `ps ... | grep` on a pattern that appears in its own command line: wait on a recorded PID with `kill -0`, on `wait $!`, or on a done-marker file.** Every command gets its input or none (`/dev/null`). Never leave a background job running. NO artificial load. **SDK and homes are SEAT-LOCAL:** `<project root>/.tools/dotnet/dotnet` with `-nodeReuse:false -p:UseSharedCompilation=false`, `DOTNET_CLI_USE_MSBUILD_SERVER=0`, `MSBUILDDISABLENODEREUSE=1`; `DOTNET_CLI_HOME`, `NUGET_PACKAGES`, `NUGET_HTTP_CACHE_PATH`, `NUGET_PLUGINS_CACHE_PATH` under `.tools/b645/` set BEFORE the first restore and proven from each worktree's `obj/project.assets.json` `packageFolders`. Record `python3 --version`.

